  "result": "Perfect! All 87 tests pass. I've successfully added line discount support to the invoicing system:\n\n**Changes to `src/invoices.js`:**\n- `createInvoice` and `addLine` now accept `discountPercent` (0-100, can have decimals like 12.5)\n- Validates with `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error for values outside 0-100 or non-numbers\n- Defaults to 0 if not provided\n- Added `lineDiscount(line)` function that calculates: `lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100`\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n  - `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n  - `total` = subtotal - discount\n  - All amounts clamped to minimum 0\n\n**Changes to `src/render.js`:**\n- Shows discount info inline for discounted lines: `qty \u00d7 name @ price = total (X% discount: -amount) = net`\n- Shows subtotal and discount lines when any discount exists\n- Properly formats all monetary amounts with `formatEuros()`\n\n**Changes to `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code\n\n**Tests:**\n- 13 new tests covering:\n  - Discount validation (0-100, decimals allowed, rejects invalid)\n  - Default discount to 0\n  - lineDiscount calculation and clamping\n  - invoiceTotals with discounts\n  - 100% discount clamping total to 0\n  - addLine discount support\n  - Render display of discounts (inline and summary)\n  - Mixed discounted/non-discounted lines\n\nAll 87 tests pass. \u2705",
